<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Shelley returns for her yearly preventive visit, six months after resection of a left convexity meningioma (CNS WHO grade 1) and on levetiracetam 500 mg twice a day. She has had no seizure since surgery and has started driving again. The stomach illness in August settled in four days. Her mood is good and she is writing every morning; she finished the first draft of her travel book last month. She completed the health risk assessment before the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Adult preventive visit, age 52</td></tr><tr><td>Active conditions</td><td>Meningioma after resection; focal epilepsy, seizure-free on levetiracetam</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Levetiracetam 500 mg twice a day; acetaminophen as needed</td></tr><tr><td>Recent events</td><td>Viral gastroenteritis in August, resolved</td></tr><tr><td>Functional status</td><td>Independent; walking most days; driving again</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient before the visit and reviewed during the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Good; better than for several years</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Close friends and her publisher; lives alone and feels safe; no financial strain; grief for old losses present but not disabling</td></tr><tr><td>Behavioral</td><td>Never smoker; a glass of wine with dinner a few times a week; walks most days; varied diet</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent in all</td></tr><tr><td>Instrumental activities of daily living</td><td>Manages her medicines with a weekly box, her money, travel, and household</td></tr><tr><td>Home safety</td><td>Smoke detector working; showers rather than baths; no falls; wears a seat belt</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>Reading glasses; eye examination last year normal</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Seven hours most nights; keeps regular hours to protect against seizures</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

